-- facts/surface-lint.rofl — THE REGISTER OF THE SURFACE LINT: the columns that name another file, and
-- the cross-file joins the JS model still keeps. Rules: examples/surface/surface.rofl. Design:
-- docs/surface-split.md, item 3.
--
-- The seeds. A column that holds a node or a path of ANOTHER file by construction: module resolution
-- (a site and the file it names) and the call edge (a site and the callee's node). Everything else that
-- is foreign-capable is derived from these through the rules' own heads.
xl_seed(module_target, 2).
xl_seed(resolved_import, 2).
xl_seed(ts_resolved, 2).
xl_seed(resolves, 2).
xl_seed(calls, 2).

-- THE BASELINE, 2026-10-05, over rules/js-*.rofl before the [surface] book: every cross-file join the
-- model makes today, one row per (head, premise). The one reason is `awaiting_rewrite`: the join goes
-- when its rule reads the other file through [surface] (docs/surface-split.md, work item 1), and the
-- row goes with it: the lint is red on a row whose finding is gone (xl_ok_stale), so a rewritten rule
-- cannot leave its excuse behind. A row for a rule that will stay is rewritten with its own reason.
-- The text names what the premise is read through: Source.Col is the foreign-capable column.

